WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.180
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday, May 28th, 2013.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:05.120
You know, something just occurred to me. I've probably said "Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday"

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:11.940
like 600 times in my life and I only just now realized that Tuesday is probably because it's the second day.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.660
Nope, in fact it is named for Tiw, the Proto-Germanic god of war.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.520
Hank, today's video comes in three parts. Part 1: A quick response to your video about Tumblr and startups

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.160
and the monetization of cool things. I think the underlying problem is that almost everything

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.820
on the Internet is dependent upon advertising and advertisers, in my opinion, are terrible at measuring

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.400
the value in the creator/viewer relationship.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.020
Hank, advertisers care much more about the number of views than the quality of views, so for instance,

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.620
Thoughts From Places videos are consistently the least viewed videos on the Vlogbrothers channel.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:46.060
So the advertising revenue model tells us to stop making Thoughts From Places videos and focus on like,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.400
giraffe sex. But in fact, Hank, we know from comments and conversations with Nerdfighters that

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.760
Thoughts From Places videos are among their favorite. The people we really want to love our videos

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.980
love those videos, dare I say it, more than giraffe sex.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.280
Now Hank, don't get me wrong. I dig giraffe sex, but I want a broader Internet. And I worry that Tumblr

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.820
and Facebook and even YouTube can only support that breadth as long as they are willing to lose money,

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.080
so Hank, please fix this problem during my paternity leave. Okay? Thanks.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:19.100
Part 2: Nerd Factor. Thank you so much to the more than 1600 people who posted videos to the Nerd Factor

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.480
competition. I am very sad that I can only be replaced by two of you. But to quote Tiw, the great Proto-Germanic

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.340
god of war, "There must always be a victor." That's not really a quote.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.380
So our first winner is MagicTurtle643!

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.920
"Check out this teacup I got. And look what it comes with. And what's this supposed to be?

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.740
A checklist? Tea, tea, tea? Well, check, check, check.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.400
Mmm, oh man, nothing in there.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.560
Look, they both have the same drowsy bear in a nightgown. And this is my personal favorite.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.640
'The Instant Chrysanthemum Beverage.' And I'm not sure if this is actually a tea or not. And I have to be honest,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.580
I haven't actually tried this one because I'm pretty sure there was a packaging error, and instead of a

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.420
chrysanthemum beverage, I wound up with packets of Chinese rat poison."

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.660
Hank, this guys been making videos for more than five years. He's participated in the Project For Awesome,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.940
and he has fewer than 700 subscribers and he's hilarious, so let's change that.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.640
So he will be playing the role of me on some forthcoming Tuesday of my paternity leave, as will

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.840
Nerdy and Quirky!

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:15.180
"Hello, welcome to Nerdy and Quirky. As a 14-year-old with the emotional maturity of, say, an unearthed potato,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:22.580
I feel like it's my responsibility to tell you all how to attract human with romantic undertones, because

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.340
Valentine's Day. *Ding*"

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.780
Nerdy and Quirky is one of the best Youtubers I have come across in years.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.400
Take a gander at this clip from her video about fangirls.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:36.820
"You may also find your fangirl in tears. Do not approach. This is their most dangerous state,

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.580
when they are prone to lash out. Take care of them from a distance.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.600
There, there, fangirl. The new season starts next fall. Unless it's from NBC."

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.500
So Hank, those are the two Nerdfighters who will be standing in for me during my paternity leave.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.620
However, I want to declare two more winners, both singers.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.960
First, Ruby Day.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:05.220
"In times like this, I wish I were a sailor, I could sail far away to hidden love.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:11.700
With the sea below and the sky above, the horizon the only thing to love, and anchors tattooed

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.960
on my chest and hands."

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.800
Oh man, that is good. And second, the Swot Sisters.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:23.000
"I am a very model of a Nerdfighter Eclectanerd. I have information, epic, awesome, literary and absurd.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.600
I play Dungeons and Dragons and I quote the Docs historical, from William Hartnell to Matt Smith,

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.940
in order categorical."

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.200
Hank, the whole song is amazing. There are links to all these channels in the dooblydoo. They are all excellent,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.980
so please check them out and subscribe to them. Thank you to everyone who submitted to Nerd Factor,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.380
and especially to Danica, who helped make all of this possible.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:42.560
And now Part 3: Hank, you remember how that special edition TFiOS audiobook, narrated by me

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.760
with, like, a bonus DVD and stuff was available for while at DFTBA.com? It is back!

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.120
Available for preorder now, link in the dooblydoo or you can just click there.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.720
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.966
Little known fact, named for Stephen Fry.

